  "change": "Per-call work in Script source-function calls. (1) ScriptAgent's depth-indexed sparse lists (sourceCallers, sourceArguments, executionContextNames) became reusable doubly linked frame chains (SourceCallFrame, ExecutionNameFrame): a call reuses the next frame, writes two fields and moves a pointer, instead of writing AVL-backed list slots. Frames are cleared on exit, so callers and legacy arguments are never retained. (2) DeclarativeEnvironment keeps its first four bindings inline (name0..3/binding0..3) and only allocates a Map for the fifth, so a function environment no longer allocates and probes a linked map per call. findBinding/bindingCount replace direct Map access in global scope, module namespace and synthetic-module readers.",
